unity Alumni Campus Resources & Services AI at Colgate Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community Request Info Visit Directory Give Home Success After Colgate National Fellowships and Scholarships Skip Sidebar Navigation In this Section In this Section Past Recipients Advising Applying About News & Updates View our list of scholarship opportunities to which our office devotes significant attention and for which Colgate has formalized application processes. Numerous awards are open to underclassmen and those seeking post-baccalaureate experiences. It is possible, and often desirable, to apply for multiple scholarships during your college years and beyond. Many of the opportunities on this page require the student to be nominated by Colgate. Application Process Advising Carefully considered, comprehensive advising is important when deciding which of these opportunities is a good fit for you and your interests, so please contact the Office of National Fellowships and Scholarships to start the conversation and application process early. Deadlines Please note that Colgate's campus deadlines are earlier — often months earlier — than the foundations' deadlines, so interested applicants should prepare well in advance. Fellowship Search Keyword Application Deadline Jan - April May - Aug Sept - Dec Current Year Of Study Alumni First-Year Student Graduate Student Junior Senior Sophomore Term of Award Academic Year Fall Multi Year None (Award Only) Spring Summer Area of Interest Africana and Latin American Studies Anthropology Arts Asian Studies Biology Chemistry Computer Science Creative Writing Economics English Environmental Film & Media Studies Geography History Humanities International Relations Mathematics Music Natural Sciences Not Discipline Specific Philosophy Physics Political Science Social Sciences Region Africa Asia and the Pacific Australia and New Zealand Europe Latin America and the Caribbean Multiple Locations Multiple Regions No travel North America The Middle East and North Africa United States American India Foundation (AIF) Banyan Impact Fellowship An immersive, 10-month volunteer service program within development organizations across India. Fellows work on scalable and sustainable development projects in the fields of education, livelihoods, and public health. Deadline: February 2025 Candidates must : ​ Be a US or Indian citizen, or a US permanent resident Be between the ages of 21 and 35 on October 1, 2025 Have completed an undergraduate or Bachelor's degree before October 1, 2025 AIF Clinton Website Amgen Scholars Program A funded life sciences summer research opportunity for undergraduate students. No prior research experience is necessary to apply for the Amgen Scholarship program. Deadline: February 1, 2025 Candidates must : Be U.S. citizens or U.S. permanent residents Be undergraduate students enrolled in accredited four-year colleges or universities in the United States, Puerto Rico, or other U.S. territories Have a cumulative grade point average of 3.2 or above Have an interest in pursuing a Ph.D. or M.D.-Ph.D Amgen Scholars Program Website Beinecke Scholarship A $35,000 award for the senior undergraduate year and graduate study in a field in which a student demonstrates unusual ability and promise. An initial grant of $5,000 is followed by a $15,000 stipend during each of the first two years of graduate study. Campus deadline: January Final deadline: March 28, 2025 Candidates must : Be an undergraduate junior at the time of application Be a US citizen or US national Plan to enter a master's or doctoral program in the arts, humanities, or social sciences Have a documented history of receiving need-based financial aid during college Be nominated by Colgate. Nomination decisions will be made by a campus committee after review of application materials submitted for the campus deadline. Beinecke Scholarship Website Current page 1 Page 2 Page 3 Page 4 Page 5 Page 6 Page 7 Page 8 … Next I