udents Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community Request Info Visit Directory Give Home Success After Colgate Outcome and Employment Data Skip Sidebar Navigation In this Section In this Section Career Development National Fellowships & Scholarships Graduate School Preparation Outcome & Employment Data Entrepreneurship & Innovation Colgate’s liberal arts approach prepares graduates for success in a wide variety of careers. Explore our students’ first post-graduate employment and continuing education outcomes. Recent Outcomes For the class of 2025, 98.8% of respondents have secured employment, graduate or professional school admission, a competitive fellowship or scholarship, or are engaged in volunteer or military service within six to nine months post-Colgate. The following dashboards allow you to explore our most recent classes’ employment, continuing education, and competitive fellowship outcomes. The content displayed represents self-reported, employer-reported, or verifiable public data gathered six to nine months following students’ graduation. Our robust knowledge rates — or the percentage of graduates for whom verifiable data exists — of at least 88% of the class allow us to tell the story of our seniors’ outcomes with confidence. 2021 2022 2023 2024 2025 Employed 76.9% 79.7% 77.0% 75.1% 74.1% Graduate Studies 21.3% 17.3% 17.4% 19.8% 23.1% Volunteer Service 0.0% 0.0% 0.3% 0.3% 0.1% Fellowships 0.5% 0.6% 1.2% 1.3% 1.1% Military 0.3% 0.0% 0.3% 0.3% 0.3% Other* 0.5% 0.2% 1.3% 0.5% 0.4% In Transition/Seeking 0.8% 1.9% 2.3% 3.0% 1.2% Total Knowledge Rate** 88.0% (618/702) 90.1% (681/756) 92.3% (684/741) 89.4% (635/710) 88.2% (740/839) * Includes travel, care for family members, etc. ** Percentage of graduates for whom verifiable self-reported, employer-reported, or public data exists six to nine months post-graduation. Individual Employment & Continuing Education Outcomes This dashboard contains specific employers and continuing education outcomes for Colgate graduates from the classes of 2016–2025. It is filterable by class year, academic division, and the academic department in which students majored or minored. Results will display graduates’ employers, graduate institutions, industries, and geographic locations of their first post-graduate outcome. Desktop dashboard Mobile dashboard Top Employer and Graduate School Information This dashboard contains the top industries, employers, graduate areas of study, and institutions attended by members of the classes of 2016–2025. It is filterable by class year, academic division, and the academic department in which students majored or minored. Desktop/tablet dashboard Mobile dashboard Recent Alumni Employment Locations Review an interactive map showing the locations of first jobs, graduate schools, fellowships, or military service outcomes for recent alumni. View map Life After Colgate You can find Colgate alumni around the world, across many industries. Eddie Brennan ’05 is president and co-owner of 1911 Established and Beak and Skiff, the fifth-generation apple orchard. Rose Gilroy ’16 got her first Hollywood job after Scarlett Johansson’s production company admired her writing samples, and hired her to write the screenplay for Fly Me to the Moon Will Vagianelis ’24 was elected fire captain for the Hamilton, N.Y. Fire Department Nicole Gordon ’10 founded Nikigo, a company that produces soy-free soy sauce and other allergy friendly Asian sauces Popular Career Fields for Recent Graduates Business/management Communications and media Consulting Education Financial Government Health and medicine Law and legal services Nonprofit and social change Sciences Sports and recreation Technology and computing Select Graduate Schools Attended by Alumni Boston College Boston University Brown University Columbia University Cornell University Harvard University New York University Rice University The University of California, Los Angeles University of Pennsylvania Washington University