ty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community Request Info Visit Directory Give Home Jobs at Colgate Live and work at one of the nation’s top liberal arts colleges. Skip Sidebar Navigation In this Section In this Section About Academics Admission & Aid Student Life Careers & Outcomes Info For The Office of Human Resources is open Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Phone: 315-228-7411 Fax: 315-228-7171 Email: humres@colgate.edu Colgate is deeply invested in employees’ success, and we all work together to ensure that students receive the premier education that is at the University’s core. Search Open Positions Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Chartwells-Colgate Dining Service Opportunities Commitment to You We work hard to provide an environment where each employee is treated as an important contributor and can continue to learn and grow. Benefits Work/Life Programs Human Resources Living the Liberal Arts Colgate is a highly selective residential liberal arts institution distinguished by academic excellence and interdisciplinary inquiry. Colgate at a Glance Academic Departments and Programs Sustainability Residential Commons Strong Sense of Place The Colgate campus, ranked as one of the most beautiful in the nation, is a place where students develop lifelong bonds with each other, faculty, and staff. Our Campus Webcams Around Colgate Village of Hamilton Colgate is located in a community of about 3,800 residents who enjoy downtown’s art galleries and restaurants and who take pride in the many historic homes and public buildings. Village of Hamilton Maps and Travel Colgate Bookstore The support and encouragement from the Colgate community was overwhelming during my entire academic career. Michael Holobosky ’19 Earned bachelor's degrees in classical studies and anthropology over 13 years. Applicants with Disabilities We are committed to facilitating a search process in which everyone can participate and barriers to access are removed to the fullest extent possible. We would welcome conversation regarding how to construct an experience that is comfortable for you and through which you will be able to show us your best. This includes, but is not limited to, providing alternative formats and/or platforms for submitting application materials, TTY or CART services, and providing information regarding the campus built environment, sensory environment, and culture. Accommodations can be arranged via Cherie Ball or Amy Ryan in the Human Resources Department. Equal Opportunity Policy The University recognizes that equal employment opportunity can only be achieved through demonstrated leadership. It is the Policy of the University to recruit, employ, retain, promote, and train employees on the basis of skills and experience, capacity to do the job, and valid job qualifications without regard to any characteristics protected by applicable local, state, or federal laws. Info For New Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community More At Colgate News Events AI Give Jobs Tools & Resources Sign In Directory Offices & Divisions Academic Calendar University Catalog Libraries Campus Services & Resources Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn 13 Oak Drive Hamilton, NY (315) 228-7000 © Colgate University Privacy Notice Non-Discrimination Policy Colgate Portal"
